**What was wrong:** Title's Position goes from 0.5 s to 1.5 s at exactly the same speed the whole way. It starts at full speed and stops dead. That's what linear keyframes do, and it's why the motion feels mechanical. Easing makes it start slowly, speed up, then slow down before it stops.

**What I just did:** I eased **Title › Position between 0.5 s and 1.5 s**. If you want it back the way it was, use **Edit > Undo**.

**What to look at:**
- Select Title and press **U** to show its keyframes. The keys at 0.5 s and 1.5 s have changed from diamonds to hourglass shapes.
- Scrub or preview from 0.5 s to 1.5 s. Title now slows into and out of the move.
- To see the curve, click the **Graph Editor** button above the timeline. It now rises gently at both ends.

**How you'll do it yourself:** select the two keys of a pair, then choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or just press **F9**.

**Your turn.** Ease the other three pairs on Title:
- **Position, 1.5 s → 3 s.** Watch out here: the key at 1.5 s looks done, but my demo only eased the side facing the first pair. Select both 1.5 s and 3 s.
- **Scale, 0.5 s → 1.5 s**
- **Opacity, 0.5 s → 1.5 s**

